  "prompt": "You are writing the control policy for a bin-sorting cell.\n\nA UR5e arm has a suction cup pointing straight down. One 40 mm cube lies on the table; it is red, green or blue.\nThree open bins stand on the table, one per colour; each is 120 x 120 mm inside, with walls 60 mm high.\nIn our test cell the cube is placed at x = 0.45 +/- 0.05 m, y = -0.05 +/- 0.05 m, yaw = 0 +/- 15 degrees.\nThe bins are fixed at red (0.25, 0.30), green (0.45, 0.30) and blue (0.65, 0.30).\nThe trial succeeds when the cube rests inside the bin of its own colour with the suction off.\n\nWrite a Python module that defines `def run(api):`. It is called once per trial and must return when\nfinished. `api` is the module below; use only these five functions (plus `math`, which you may import).\nYou have at most 300 API calls per trial. Contact force on the pad above 150 N aborts the trial as a collision.\n\n```python\n\"\"\"The five functions a sorting policy may call. A policy is `def run(api): ...` and receives this module.\n\nUnits: metres and degrees in the world frame; z is up and the table top is z = 0.\nThe robot has a suction cup pointing straight down. The centre of its 28 x 28 mm square pad is the controlled\npoint. One 40 mm cube lies on the table; its colour is red, green or blue. Three open bins stand on the table,\none per colour. Each bin is 120 x 120 mm inside, with 60 mm high walls. The trial succeeds when the cube\nrests inside the bin of its own colour with the suction off.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\n_SIM = None  # set by the trial runner\n\n\ndef cube_pose():\n    \"\"\"Camera estimate of the cube: returns ((x, y, z_top_face), yaw_deg, colour).\n    Yaw is the rotation of the cube about z, reported in [-45, 45) because a square repeats every 90 degrees.\n    colour is \"red\", \"green\" or \"blue\".\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.cube_pose()\n\n\ndef bin_pose(colour):\n    \"\"\"Camera estimate of the bin for colour (\"red\", \"green\" or \"blue\"): returns ((x, y, z_rim), yaw_deg).\n    (x, y) is the centre of the bin floor; z_rim is the height of the top of its walls.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.bin_pose(colour)\n\n\ndef move_to(xyz, yaw_deg):\n    \"\"\"Move the pad centre to xyz (metres) with the pad rotated yaw_deg about z, cup pointing down.\n    Joint-space motion; blocks until the arm has settled. A held cube moves with the cup.\n    The run is aborted as a collision if the contact force on the pad ever exceeds 150 N.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.move_to(xyz, yaw_deg)\n\n\ndef suction(on):\n    \"\"\"Switch the vacuum on (True) or off (False), then wait for things to settle.\n    The pad grips only what it touches. Returns True if the cup now holds the cube, else False.\n    Switching off releases the cube, which drops from where it is.\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.suction(on)\n\n\ndef done():\n    \"\"\"True if the cube rests inside the bin of its own colour (each bin has a load cell).\"\"\"\n    return _SIM.done()\n\n```\n\nReply with the complete module in a single ```python code block, followed by at most three sentences\nexplaining the strategy.",
  "response": "```python\n\"\"\"Colour sorting with aligned pickup and clearance-height transport.\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\n\ndef run(api):\n    bins = {\"red\", \"green\", \"blue\"}\n\n    def segment(start, end, yaw, spacing=0.01):\n        \"\"\"Use short waypoint moves to limit joint-space path excursions.\"\"\"\n        distance = math.sqrt(sum((end[i] - start[i]) ** 2 for i in range(3)))\n        count = max(1, int(math.ceil(distance / spacing)))\n        for k in range(1, count + 1):\n            t = k / count\n            point = tuple(start[i] + t * (end[i] - start[i])\n                          for i in range(3))\n            api.move_to(point, yaw)\n        return end\n\n    api.suction(False)\n\n    # Two bounded attempts leave ample room within the 300-call budget.\n    for _ in range(2):\n        (x, y, top), yaw, colour = api.cube_pose()\n        if colour not in bins:\n            return\n\n        (bx, by, rim), _ = api.bin_pose(colour)\n        clearance = max(0.20, rim + 0.12, top + 0.12)\n\n        position = (x, y, clearance)\n        api.move_to(position, yaw)\n        position = segment(position, (x, y, top + 0.003), yaw)\n\n        held = False\n        # Align the square pad with the cube and approach in 0.25 mm steps.\n        # Limit the nominal compression to 0.5 mm.\n        for k in range(15):\n            position = (x, y, top + 0.003 - 0.00025 * k)\n            api.move_to(position, yaw)\n            if api.suction(True):\n                held = True\n                break\n\n        if not held:\n            api.suction(False)\n            segment(position, (x, y, clearance), yaw)\n            continue\n\n        # Lift before moving toward any bin walls.\n        position = segment(position, (x, y, clearance), yaw)\n        position = segment(position, (bx, by, clearance), yaw)\n\n        # The cube's bottom remains 10 mm above the rim at release.\n        # Dropping centrally avoids inserting the cup into the bin.\n        position = segment(position, (bx, by, rim + 0.050), yaw)\n        api.suction(False)\n        api.done()\n        return\n```\n\nThe policy aligns the pad to the cube, confirms suction during a fine-step approach, and transports only after lifting clear of the walls. It releases centrally just above the correct bin and uses fewer than 300 API calls in the stated cell. The API provides no force feedback or camera-error bounds, so collision avoidance cannot be guaranteed under arbitrary estimation errors.",
  "code": "\"\"\"Colour sorting with aligned pickup and clearance-height transport.\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\n\ndef run(api):\n    bins = {\"red\", \"green\", \"blue\"}\n\n    def segment(start, end, yaw, spacing=0.01):\n        \"\"\"Use short waypoint moves to limit joint-space path excursions.\"\"\"\n        distance = math.sqrt(sum((end[i] - start[i]) ** 2 for i in range(3)))\n        count = max(1, int(math.ceil(distance / spacing)))\n        for k in range(1, count + 1):\n            t = k / count\n            point = tuple(start[i] + t * (end[i] - start[i])\n                          for i in range(3))\n            api.move_to(point, yaw)\n        return end\n\n    api.suction(False)\n\n    # Two bounded attempts leave ample room within the 300-call budget.\n    for _ in range(2):\n        (x, y, top), yaw, colour = api.cube_pose()\n        if colour not in bins:\n            return\n\n        (bx, by, rim), _ = api.bin_pose(colour)\n        clearance = max(0.20, rim + 0.12, top + 0.12)\n\n        position = (x, y, clearance)\n        api.move_to(position, yaw)\n        position = segment(position, (x, y, top + 0.003), yaw)\n\n        held = False\n        # Align the square pad with the cube and approach in 0.25 mm steps.\n        # Limit the nominal compression to 0.5 mm.\n        for k in range(15):\n            position = (x, y, top + 0.003 - 0.00025 * k)\n            api.move_to(position, yaw)\n            if api.suction(True):\n                held = True\n                break\n\n        if not held:\n            api.suction(False)\n            segment(position, (x, y, clearance), yaw)\n            continue\n\n        # Lift before moving toward any bin walls.\n        position = segment(position, (x, y, clearance), yaw)\n        position = segment(position, (bx, by, clearance), yaw)\n\n        # The cube's bottom remains 10 mm above the rim at release.\n        # Dropping centrally avoids inserting the cup into the bin.\n        position = segment(position, (bx, by, rim + 0.050), yaw)\n        api.suction(False)\n        api.done()\n        return\n",
